<%- contentFor('body') %>

<!-- PROJECT 1 -->
<div class="card rounded border border-dark border-4" style="width: 25rem;">
<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column align-items-center p-3">
<h2>Building a Network</h2>
<img src="/images/project 1.png" alt="1st Project" width="300" height="239" class="container-fluid d-flex flex-column align-items-center">
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#project1Modal">More Details</button>

<div class="modal fade" id="project1Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="project1ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">

        <div class="modal-dialog modal-fullscreen">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                      <h5 class="modal-title" id="project1ModalLabel">Building a Network</h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p>
                        One of my favourite projects was during my 1st year 2nd semester Networking course. We were tasked with creating an entire networking system for 3 buildings that were connected via a single router. From configuring the IP addresses to making sure each device could communicate with each other, this project was all around engaging. The best part about it was the finished product in which every single device could ping each other. This really helped improve my critical thinking skills since it required extensive focus to be completed.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>


<!-- PROJECT 2 -->
<div class="card rounded border border-dark border-4" style="width: 25rem;">
<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column align-items-center p-3">
<h2>Advanced Networks: Static Routes</h2>
<img src="/images/project 2.jpg" alt="2nd Project" width="300" height="200" class="container-fluid d-flex flex-column align-items-center">
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#project2Modal">More Details</button>

<div class="modal fade" id="project2Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="project2ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">

        <div class="modal-dialog modal-fullscreen">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                      <h5 class="modal-title" id="project2ModalLabel">Advanced Networks: Static Routes</h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p>
                    The hardest project I've done was somewhat similar to the previous 
                    project, but with much more devices to configure as well as extra tasks. 
                    Not only did we have to create the entire network, but we also had to 
                    configure static IP's so that the devices could connect to remote servers.
                    This was the most challenging because there were so many errors throughout, 
                    but at the end of the day, it was a great learning experience for me and my 
                    partners. It taught me a lot.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- PROJECT 3 -->
<div class="card rounded border border-dark border-4" style="width: 25rem;">
<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column align-items-center p-3">
<h2>Login Database</h2>
<img src="/images/{part 1} project 4.png" alt="3rd Project" width="300" height="180">
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#project3Modal">More Details</button>

<div class="modal fade" id="project3Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="project3ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">

        <div class="modal-dialog modal-fullscreen">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                      <h5 class="modal-title" id="project3ModalLabel">Login Database</h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p>
                    This project was one I found really fun to do and it allowed me to 
                    really find my love for coding. At the time it seemed difficult, 
                    but looking back now, I realise it was relatively simple. We were 
                    tasked with creating a student ledger that displays details about 
                    students. This included a login page, a menu page, as well as the 
                    information page. The students would enter their information, and 
                    the system would save it to a local database. This way, anytime it 
                    was to be accessed, it can be pulled from the database. This was and 
                    is still one of the coolest projects I've done as it had real-world 
                    application and proved how easy it is to code such complex looking things.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- PROJECT 4 -->
<div class="card rounded border border-dark border-4" style="width: 25rem;">
<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column align-items-center p-3">
<h2>Grade Calculator</h2>
<img src="/images/{part 2} project 4.png" alt="4th Project" width="300" height="200">
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#project4Modal">More Details</button>

<div class="modal fade" id="project4Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="project4ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">

        <div class="modal-dialog modal-fullscreen">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                      <h5 class="modal-title" id="project4ModalLabel">Grade Calculator</h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p>
                    A project that I still use till this day would be the grade calculator 
                    we were assigned to make in high school. In my final year of highschool, 
                    we were given a project to create absolutely anything we wanted, as long 
                    as it followed a specific set of rules. I chose to create a grade calculator 
                    that calculated averages, and my favourite part, how much you'd need to score 
                    on an exam to get the grade you want. Obviously there are sites that do it better 
                    like Calculator.net, but the one I made really was monumental for me because 
                    I managed to code it from complete scratch. This really gave me confidence to 
                    pursue coding at a higher level and had quite an impact on my major in University. 
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
